{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3275","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3275","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3275\",\"parent_revision\":\"134f77974f94f9f4a93a46857bb3ebc7608252a3\",\"root_revision\":\"41f48e1dbf1c835cb03897cd2acf46bbee04e7bac07fbe783a266b0f1a6b92a1\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-28\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe backlog MCP tools are meant to be provider-neutral \u2014 the configured backend can be GitHub, Beads, SQLite, or Memory (confirmed: `SyncProvider` protocol at `backlog_core/backend_types.py:203` is used throughout `operations.py`, e.g. lines 1168, 1596, 3079, 3739, 3816, 3875, 3925, specifically to gate cache/reconciliation behavior in a backend-agnostic way, cleanly no-oping with \\\"Active backend does not support reconciliation.\\\" for backends that have no cache).\\n\\nDespite that, `backlog_list`'s cache-refresh parameter is named `from_github` (`backlog_core/server.py:1936`), naming one specific backend in a tool meant to work across all of them. The sibling reconcile/pull tool already uses a provider-neutral name for the equivalent concept (`full_refresh`, `server.py:1624`), so the naming is inconsistent even within the existing surface, not just non-neutral in isolation.\\n\\nSeparately, `backlog_view` has no bypass-cache option at all \u2014 its full parameter set (`selector`, `head`, `include_content`, `limit`, `map`, `navigate`, `offset`, `section`, `sections`, `show`, `since`, `skip_tokens`, `summary`) contains nothing equivalent to `from_github`/`full_refresh`. It always reads local cache with no way to ask it to check the live backend first.\\n\\nThis caused a real problem this session: while trying to verify whether recently-groomed content had actually reached GitHub, `backlog_view` could not answer the question \u2014 it would show correctly-synced-looking content regardless of whether anything had actually reached the remote backend, because it never consults the backend directly. Confirming required going outside the tool surface entirely (shelling out to `gh issue view`), and even that took multiple attempts to get right, because it wasn't obvious which of GitHub's own fields corresponds to what this system treats as authoritative.\\n\\nWhat a working fix has to do, stated as outcomes rather than implementation: give every backlog command that reads cached data a consistent way to bypass that cache and validate against the raw backend, named without reference to any specific backend; and make `backlog_view` support it, not just `backlog_list`. A correct implementation must not read a backend's raw storage naively \u2014 for GitHub specifically, the visible issue body is not the authoritative record (see `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` lines 780-789: the issue body is deliberately never overwritten, and the authoritative content lives in an append-only audit-comment record resolved via a head pointer) \u2014 so a live-check option has to go through the same resolution path the existing reconciliation logic already uses, not shortcut around it by reading a backend's most obvious-looking field directly.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T14:53:05.105477Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: feat: backlog_list's `from_github` parameter is GitHub-specific on a provider-neutral tool, and no backlog command can bypass cache to validate against the raw backend\\nDate: 2026-08-29\\nGoal: Give every backlog command that reads cached data a consistent, provider-neutral way to bypass the cache and validate against the raw backend, and add that capability to backlog_view, which currently has none.\\nConditions:\\n1. Current locations/behavior of `from_github` (server.py:1936) and the provider-neutral sibling `full_refresh` (server.py:1624) are known | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. GitHub's backend-authoritative resolution path (audit-comment record via head pointer, not the raw issue body) is documented in ARCHITECTURE.md:780-789 | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. Full inventory of which backlog commands besides list/view read cached/stale data (candidates gated by SyncProvider checkpoint logic in operations.py near lines 1168, 1596, 3079, 3739, 3816, 3875, 3925) | Status: DERIVABLE\\n4. Whether `from_github` has any existing internal callers (repo code, docs, or skills) that would break on a rename vs. needing a deprecated alias | Status: DERIVABLE\\n5. Which existing reconciliation function performs the GitHub head-pointer resolution and can be reused (rather than rebuilt) for a live-view path on backlog_view | Status: DERIVABLE\\nAVAILABLE count: 2\\nDERIVABLE count: 3\\nMISSING count: 0\\n</div>\\n\\n## Research\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T14:58:04.936832Z</sub>\\n\\n**Codebase audit (backlog_core/server.py + operations.py + backends/github_*.py)**\\n\\n**(a) `from_github` and `full_refresh` already share the same underlying function.**\\n- `backlog_list`'s `from_github` (server.py:1936) flows through `operations.list_items(from_github=...)` (operations.py:1766-1807), which \u2014 when `from_github=True` \u2014 calls `operations.refresh_local_cache_from_github()` (operations.py:1572-1612).\\n- `sync_now`'s `full_refresh` (server.py:1624) flows through `_sync_engine._startup_sync_loop(full_refresh=...)` \u2192 `_attempt_sync` \u2192 `_run_single_sync` (sync_engine.py:92-110), which calls the **exact same function**: `operations.refresh_local_cache_from_github(full_refresh=...)`.\\n- Inside that shared function, `full_refresh` just selects `ReconcileScope.INITIAL` vs `.INCREMENTAL` (operations.py:1599), then calls `backend.reconcile(ReconcileRequest(scope=..., ...))` \u2014 the one reconciliation entry point every cache-refreshing tool in this file uses (also used by `sync_items`, `pull_by_selector`, `pull_items`, `_reconcile_groomed_item`, `backlog_strike_entry`).\\n- `from_github` on `backlog_list` is effectively \\\"incremental full_refresh\\\"; the two parameters are the same knob at different granularity, not independent mechanisms. A rename to a provider-neutral name (e.g. `refresh_cache` or `live` to match `full_refresh`'s neutral phrasing) does not require touching this shared plumbing \u2014 only the MCP-facing `Annotated` parameter name/description on `backlog_list` (server.py:1936) and its docstring at server.py:2104, plus the internal `from_github` kwarg name on `operations.list_items` (operations.py:1767, 1782, 1806) if full consistency is wanted.\\n\\n**(b) The audit-comment/head-pointer resolution is already a single shared function \u2014 `backlog_view` already calls it, but only conditionally.**\\n- The authoritative-content resolver is `GitHubWorkItems.work_item_version()` (backends/github_work_items.py:341+). It is the ONE place that reads the Contents-API head record + validates the audit comment (ARCHITECTURE.md:780-789).\\n- It already has exactly two callers, both already reused, no extraction needed:\\n  1. **Write/reconcile path**: `provider_item_from_issue()` (github_work_items.py:316-338) calls `work_item_version()` and feeds `_fetch_snapshot()` \u2192 `reconcile()` (github_work_items.py:471-530) \u2014 this is what `from_github`/`full_refresh` ultimately execute.\\n  2. **View path**: `GitHubBackend.view_enrich_from_github()` (backends/github_backend.py:546-561) passes `resolve_version=lambda ...: self._work_items.work_item_version(...)[0]` into `gh_client.view_enrich_from_github()` (gh_client.py:1716-1763), which uses it to resolve `body` from the head record instead of the raw issue body (gh_client.py:1746-1748), with graceful fallback to raw body on `ContentConflictError`/`ContentUnavailableError`.\\n- Critically: `operations.view_item()` (operations.py:2854-2933) **already calls `view_enrich_from_github()` unconditionally** whenever the selector parses to a numeric issue reference (`issue_num = parse_issue_selector(selector)`, operations.py:2913, 2917-2926) \u2014 this is an uncontrolled live GitHub network call today, not a cache-only read, for that selector shape.\\n- The actual gap: this live call only fires when `parse_issue_selector(selector)` succeeds, i.e. the selector *itself* is a URL/`#N`/bare number. When a caller passes a **title substring** (or, on the beads backend, a nanoid not already found locally) and a local item IS found by title match, `view_item()` takes the `elif not item:` branch and skips straight to returning cached/local data \u2014 no live enrichment happens, and there is no parameter to force it. So `backlog_view` doesn't \\\"entirely lack\\\" live-check capability as the item's framing states \u2014 it has an *implicit, unconditional, selector-shape-gated* live check for numeric selectors, and *no* mechanism at all for title-selector or explicitly-requested bypass. The fix needed is smaller than \\\"add live-check from scratch\\\": expose the existing conditional as an explicit parameter (e.g. `bypass_cache: bool`) that (1) forces the `view_enrich_from_github` path even for title selectors that resolved locally, and (2) is honest in its default (today's unconditional call for numeric selectors arguably should also move behind this flag for symmetry with `backlog_list`, since it currently makes an uncontrolled network round-trip on every view-by-number call).\\n\\n**(c) MCP tools that read local cache \u2014 bypass-cache candidates vs. mutate-only tools.**\\nEnumerated all `@mcp.tool` functions in server.py (grep for `@mcp.tool`/`async def`):\\n- **Cache-read, no bypass today (candidates for the same capability):**\\n  - `backlog_view` (server.py:2392) \u2014 see (b) above.\\n  - `backlog_list_followups` (server.py:2740) \u2192 `operations.list_followups()` reads `list_work_items()` directly, no `from_github`-equivalent parameter at all. Same class of gap as `backlog_view`, not explicitly named in the item but structurally identical (derived filter over the same cache).\\n- **Cache-read, bypass already exists:**\\n  - `backlog_list` (server.py:1935) \u2014 `from_github` (subject of this item's rename ask).\\n- **Mutate-then-reconcile (not a \\\"list against cache\\\" concern, reconciliation is inherent to the write, not optional):**\\n  - `sync_now`, `backlog_sync` \u2192 `sync_items()` (operations.py:3065-3099), `backlog_pull` \u2192 `pull_by_selector`/`pull_items` (operations.py:3829-3939, already TARGETED-scope reconcile against the live backend by construction), `backlog_close`, `backlog_resolve`, `backlog_update`, `backlog_groom` (triggers `_reconcile_groomed_item`, operations.py:1166-1178), `backlog_strike_entry` (operations.py:3736-3741, targeted reconcile after mutation), `backlog_add`, `backlog_normalize`, `backlog_create_sam_task`, `backlog_update_sam_task_status`.\\n  - `backlog_get_sam_tasks` / `backlog_get_ready_sam_tasks` \u2014 different subsystem (SAM plan tasks), not backlog item cache.\\n  - `artifact_register`/`artifact_list`/`artifact_get`/`artifact_read` \u2014 separate content-provider subsystem, not the backlog item cache/reconciliation path this item concerns.\\n  - `sync_status` \u2014 reads in-memory sync state only, no cache/backend read.\\n- **Conclusion for scope**: only `backlog_view` and `backlog_list_followups` are genuine \\\"reads cached data, no live-check option\\\" gaps besides `backlog_list` (already has one). `backlog_pull` already provides a raw-backend-bypass write path per selector but returns only a file_path/diff, not the item content itself \u2014 so it does not substitute for a `backlog_view` live flag; the item's ask to add the capability directly to `backlog_view` (rather than \\\"call pull first, then view\\\") is the right shape. `backlog_list_followups` is a plausible secondary target but is out of the item's stated scope (title only names `backlog_list` and `backlog_view`); flagging it for the groomer/planner to explicitly include or defer.\\n\\n**(d) Rename safety \u2014 no production caller breaks; only the internal `operations.list_items` kwarg and docs are affected.**\\n- Grep for `from_github` across the plugin found only ONE production (non-test, non-generated) call site passing it as a keyword argument: `sam_schema/backlog.py:95` \u2014 `operations.list_items(from_github=refresh, ...)`. This calls the **internal `operations.list_items()` function directly**, not the MCP tool `backlog_list`. Renaming only the MCP-surface `Annotated` parameter on `server.py`'s `backlog_list` (line 1936) does not break this caller.\\n- If the rename is also propagated to `operations.list_items`'s own `from_github` parameter (operations.py:1767) for full naming consistency, `sam_schema/backlog.py:95` would need updating (one call site, one keyword) \u2014 low blast radius, no deprecation alias needed since this is a single internal caller within the same plugin, not a published/external API.\\n- Documentation that references `from_github` and would go stale on rename (non-blocking, but should be updated in the same change): `skills/backlog/SKILL.md:54` (parameter table), `skills/backlog/README.md:224,253,283` (usage example + prose), and the generated `docs/dh-workflow-graph.json` / `docs/workflow-layers/G8-backend-routing.json` (regenerable via `dh:meta-workflow-graph-refresh`, not hand-maintained).\\n- No CLI flag (e.g. `--from-github`) exists anywhere in server.py \u2014 this is an MCP-tool-only parameter, so no shell-script/CI callers are at risk.\\n- All other hits for `from_github` are either test files (`tests/`, `tests_backlog/`, `backlog_core/tests/`) exercising the parameter directly and will need their keyword-arg names updated alongside the rename, or unrelated symbols that merely contain the substring (`refresh_local_cache_from_github`, `view_enrich_from_github`, `fetch_tasks_from_github` in `implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py` \u2014 a different, unrelated function name, not a caller of `backlog_list`'s parameter).\\n\\n**Net implication for planning**: this item is a naming/API-surface change plus a genuinely small feature addition, not a new subsystem. No new reconciliation logic needs to be built \u2014 `work_item_version()` and `reconcile()` already exist and are already shared. The task decomposes into: (1) rename `backlog_list`'s `from_github` \u2192 neutral name (server.py:1936, operations.py:1767/1782/1806, docs), (2) add an explicit bypass-cache parameter to `backlog_view` that calls `view_enrich_from_github()` (already reused, no extraction) unconditionally on request \u2014 including for title-resolved selectors, which today never get it \u2014 and (3) decide (a planning-time decision, not research) whether to also gate today's unconditional numeric-selector live call behind the same flag for consistent, predictable cache-vs-live semantics.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 confusion while investigating whether #3169/#3268 grooming had reached GitHub\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-28\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"47d4e627ccd873f7526581fcbe960ebaf1cd6228c06dfcc5e160367d4c9b4c75\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRRbnxg\"}"}